{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Everything's set up. I've done three things for you:\n\n1. **Removed `>/dev/null 2>&1`** from `~/.gemini/settings.json` so hook errors are now visible (backup at `~/.gemini/settings.json.cledger-smoke-backup`). Left Qwen's redirect alone — Test 5 exists to verify it.\n2. **Wrote `~/tmp/cledger-check.mjs`** — a checker that prints PASS/FAIL so you never read raw JSON.\n3. **Found your local gateway** running at `127.0.0.1:8001` with `deepseek-v4-flash` (tool-calling supported), so the Qwen tests cost you nothing.\n\nI'll hold off running `npm test` in the worktree until you say you're done, so no rebuild can race your hooks.\n\n---\n\n# Test 2 — Gemini `/rewind`\n\n**Step 1.** Open a terminal:\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke\ngemini\n```\n\n**Step 2.** Type this and press Enter. **Wait for the full answer.**\n```\nwhat is 2+2?\n```\n\n**Step 3.** Type this and press Enter. **Wait for the full answer.**\n```\nwhat is 10+10?\n```\n\n**Step 4.** Type and press Enter:\n```\n/rewind\n```\n\n**Step 5.** A dialog opens listing your messages. Use ↑/↓ to highlight **`what is 2+2?`** and press Enter.\n\n**Step 6.** ⚠️ You'll be offered three choices. Pick **\"Rewind conversation\"**.\n\nDo *not* pick \"Revert code changes\" — that only touches files and writes no rewind record, so the test would falsely fail.\n\n**Step 7.** Type `/quit`, then run:\n```bash\nnode ~/tmp/cledger-check.mjs 2\n```\n\n**Expected:**\n```\n  PASS  1 rewind activity/activities recorded\n        seq=N withdrew 2 message(s): [...]\n  PASS  every withdrawn message is still captured as a turn (union capture holds)\n```\n\nThat second line is the whole thesis of this adapter — Gemini threw the messages away, the ledger kept them *and* recorded that they were withdrawn.\n\n---\n\n# Test 3 — the catch-up sweep\n\nThis needs **two terminals**. It's the feature I un-broke, and it has never once run successfully.\n\n**Step 1.** Terminal A:\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke\ngemini\n```\n\n**Step 2.** Ask it something and **let the answer finish completely**:\n```\nwrite a haiku about git\n```\n⚠️ Waiting matters. The hook must capture this session once, or the sweep will correctly ignore it later.\n\n**Step 3.** Open **Terminal B** and find the process:\n```bash\npgrep -fl gemini\n```\nCopy the number at the start of the gemini line, then:\n```bash\nkill -9 <that-number>\n```\nTerminal A should die instantly. That's the point — `SessionEnd` never fires, so the file's tail is stranded.\n\n**Step 4.** In Terminal B, take the snapshot:\n```bash\nnode ~/tmp/cledger-check.mjs 3a\n```\n\n**Step 5.** Start a second session and quit it normally:\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke\ngemini\n```\nAsk `hello`, wait for the reply, then type `/quit`.\n\n**Step 6.**\n```bash\nnode ~/tmp/cledger-check.mjs 3b\n```\n\n**Expected:** the killed session's count **grows** (`12 -> 14`):\n```\n  PASS  1 previously-captured session(s) grew — the sweep picked up the stranded tail\n```\n\nIf it says FAIL, the sweep still isn't finding cursors and I need to look again.\n\n---\n\n# Test 4 — Qwen subagents, `@file`, titles\n\n**Step 1.** New terminal, point Qwen at your local model:\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke\nexport OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1\nexport OPENAI_API_KEY=dummy\nexport OPENAI_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash\nqwen\n```\n(If Qwen asks how to authenticate, choose the **OpenAI** option.)\n\n**Step 2.** Type each of these, waiting for each to finish:\n```\nsummarize @calc.py\n```\n```\n/chat save smoke-test\n```\n```\n/agents\n```\nCreate a simple agent and let it run once. If `/agents` is confusing or won't run one, skip it — the other two still matter, and I'll note subagents as unverified.\n\n**Step 3.** Type `/quit`, then:\n```bash\nnode ~/tmp/cledger-check.mjs 4\n```\n\n**Expected:** PASS on `context_injection` (from `@calc.py`), PASS on `custom_title` (from `/chat save`), PASS on a sub-conversation if you ran an agent, and **PASS on \"no format drift