{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Fixes are committed and pushed. Here's where things stand and what I need from you.\n\n## What I fixed (`3eeeada`, pushed to `worktree-more-cli-adapters`)\n\nAll four verified against your real Gemini session, not just synthetic fixtures:\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Sweep cursor key** | cursor written under `63ca4425-bedf-…`, sweep looked up `session-2026-08-04T03-54-63ca4425` → skipped every session forever | keyed by file name — the only id the sweep has before reading |\n| **Cursor monotonicity** | 4-record file left the cursor at `1` | reaches `7` on your real 5-line session |\n| **Snapshot drop** | `rewound` computed, never emitted; the recovered prompt looked ordinary | `seq=5 activity/snapshot_drop removed=[\"ba071351-…\"]` — that's exactly the `hi` at seq 3 |\n| **`raw` bloat** | each `session_state` stored the whole conversation (916 B of a 2.2 KB session, ×2) | 92 B; messages keep their own verbatim raw |\n\nPlus: `--all` now names the directory it searched instead of a silent `+0 events`.\n\nTests: **200, 199 pass / 1 pre-existing skip**, three new Gemini tests covering the cursor key, the drop, and the raw pruning. I did *not* touch the qwen timestampless-line drop — it matches claude-code's existing convention, so changing it is a cross-adapter decision, not a bug fix.\n\nOne judgment call to veto if you disagree: pruning `$set.messages` from stored `raw` is the first place an adapter doesn't keep the source line verbatim. I think the amplification earns it and nothing is lost, but it's your principle.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Read this first or every smoke test will fail\n\nYour global `cledger` is **0.18.0**, symlinked to the *main* checkout. It doesn't know these adapters:\n\n```\n$ echo '{}' | cledger hook gemini-cli\nunknown hook source: gemini-cli\n```\n\nAnd because `install` added `>/dev/null 2>&1`, **your installed Gemini and Qwen hooks are currently silent no-ops.** Point the global binary at the branch first:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters\nnpm link\ncledger --version          # must print 0.20.0\n```\n\nRevert when done: `cd ~/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger && npm link`.\n\nNote this also routes your live **claude-code** capture through branch code until you revert. It passes the full suite, but it is a real side effect.\n\nThen make a scratch repo (capture needs a git repo with a commit, and Gemini scopes chats to the directory you launch it in — always run `cledger` from the same directory):\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/tmp/cledger-smoke && cd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke\ngit init && printf 'def add(a, b):\\n    return a + b\\n' > calc.py\ngit add -A && git commit -m init\n```\n\nInspection command for every test below (machinery kinds are hidden by default):\n\n```bash\ncledger log --with-state --source gemini-cli     # or --source qwen-code\ncledger log --with-state --source gemini-cli --json | less   # to see blocks\n```\n\n---\n\n## Test 1 — Gemini model turn with tool calls · **highest value**\n\nNothing has ever exercised this. Your only real Gemini session has **zero model turns** — `modelBlocks`, `thoughts`, `toolCalls`, tool results, and the settledness hold are synthetic-test-only.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke && gemini\n> read calc.py and explain what it does, then add a subtract function\n> /quit\ncledger log --with-state --source gemini-cli --json | less\n```\n\n**Pass:** an `actor.type: \"agent\"` turn exists; its `blocks` run `thinking` → `text` → `tool_use` → `tool_result`; **each tool call appears exactly once**; every model reply you saw on screen is present.\n\n**Fail signals:** each `tool_use` appearing *twice* means the `callsInContent` precedence branch is wrong. A model turn missing entirely means the settledness hold is stuck — check `cledger log --json` for a cursor that never advanced.\n\n## Test 2 — Gemini `/rewind`\n\nThe only path that fires the `rewind` activity, and it's never run against real data.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke && gemini\n> what is 2+2?\n> what is 3+3?\n> /rewind          # pick the 2+2 turn\n> /quit\ncledger log --with-state --source gemini-cli\n```\n\n**Pass:** an `activity/rewind` naming the withdrawn ids, **and the rewound turns still present** as turns. Both halves matter — that's the whole union-capture thesis.\n\n## Test 3 — Gemini sweep · **newly un-broken, never run**\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke && gemini\n> write a haiku about git\n```\nNow **`kill -9`** the gemini process from another terminal (so `SessionEnd` never fires), then:\n```bash\ngemini\n> hello\n> /quit\ncledger log --with-state --source gemini-cli\n```\n\n**Pass:** the haiku session's turns appear, picked up by the second session's sweep. **Fail:** only the second session is present — the sweep is still not finding cursors.\n\n## Test 4 — Qwen subagents, `@file`, titles\n\nYour 19 local Qwen sessions contain only `user`/`assistant`/`tool_result`/`ui_telemetry`/`attribution_snapshot`. Every other subtype mapping is read off Qwen's source list, never off a transcript.\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke && qwen\n> summarize @calc.py           # → context_injection / at_command\n> /agents                      # create + run one → parent_session, agent_launch_prompt\n> /chat save smoke-test        # → session_state / custom_title\n> /quit\ncledger log --with-state --source qwen-code\ncledger conversations\n```\n\n**Pass:** a `context_injection`; a **second conversation** whose `parent` is the main one; a `session_state/custom_title`. **Fail:** subagent turns landing in the parent conversation, or anything showing up as `unrecognized` (that's a drift warning worth telling me about).\n\n## Test 5 — Qwen headless, re-confirm the detach\n\n```bash\ncd ~/tmp/cledger-smoke && qwen -p \"say hi in one word\"\ncledger log --with-state --source qwen-code\n```\n\n**Pass:** the turn is captured. This is the case `>/dev/null 2>&1` exi