{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"You hit a server-side entitlement change, not a format change. Here's what I verified:\n\n**The rejection isn't in the client.** I grepped the 0.54.0 bundle — that message string doesn't exist locally, so it came from Google's OAuth endpoint. They turned off free Code Assist for individuals on this client; the CLI itself is unchanged and still shipping (it auto-updated 0.53.1 → 0.54.0 while we were working).\n\n**Answering your three questions:**\n\n**1. Do you need an API key?** It's the simplest path, but you have four options — only `oauth-personal` got cut. The shipped 0.54.0 still supports `gemini-api-key`, `vertex-ai`, and `cloud-shell`. An AI Studio key in `GEMINI_API_KEY` is the two-minute fix. (I can't confirm current AI Studio free-tier terms from this machine — you'll know immediately when you try.)\n\n**2. Switch to Antigravity's CLI?** No. This is billing, not deprecation. Gemini CLI is still published and its transcript format is untouched.\n\n**3. Support both?** Not now, and I'd resist building it speculatively. If Antigravity ships its own local transcript store, that's a *new adapter* alongside gemini-cli — the opencode/claude-code relationship — not a replacement. I genuinely don't know whether it has a CLI or what its storage looks like, and this PR's own bar is that every format claim comes from a live transcript or shipped source rather than inference. Put it on the TODO adapter list; build it when you have it installed and I can read a real session file.\n\n**Free drift check from the auto-update:** I re-verified the adapter against 0.54.0. `isRewindRecord`, `isMessageRecord`, `isMetadataUpdateRecord`, and `isPartialMetadataRecord` are byte-identical to 0.53.1. **The adapter needs no changes for the new version.**\n\n**One thing this explains.** The PR body says both CLIs were \"driven against a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint.\" That can't be true for Gemini — it has no OpenAI mode (only `GOOGLE_GEMINI_BASE_URL`, which expects a Gemini-shaped API). Qwen does have `OPENAI_API_KEY`/`OPENAI_BASE_URL`, which is how it got 19 real sessions while Gemini got one with zero model turns and a failed call. So the snapshot-drop incident that motivated the union-capture design was very likely triggered by that endpoint mismatch. The design still stands — API failures from quota or 500s are ordinary, and the README already says \"after a failed API call\" — but that's the provenance.\n\nneeds input: which auth path you want for the Gemini smoke tests — I can't create an API key for you.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","head":"2f470e288b3f8620dfc20ca4011ceaee4f18c8f9","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-5d7216e0c60259459ec31841c5561ba6918191640a39f97724e1c3322d53ad8d","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"d10310cd-8144-4046-87b9-97bbb6ace18c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.223"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-06T05:20:51.196Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/more-cli-adapters","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-more-cli-adapters","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"You hit a server-side entitlement change, not a format change. Here's what I verified:\n\n**The rejection isn't in the client.** I grepped the 0.54.0 bundle — that message string doesn't exist locally, so it came from Google's OAuth endpoint. They turned off free Code Assist for individuals on this client; the CLI itself is unchanged and still shipping (it auto-updated 0.53.1 → 0.54.0 while we were working).\n\n**Answering your three questions:**\n\n**1. Do you need an API key?** It's the simplest path, bu